  "question": {
    "text": "The $\\mathrm{pK}_{\\mathrm{a}}$ of a weak acid, $\\mathrm{HA}$, is $4.80$. The $\\mathrm{pK}_{\\mathrm{b}}$ of a weak base, $\\mathrm{BOH}$, is $4.78$. The $\\mathrm{pH}$ of an aqueous solution of the corresponding salt, BA, will be",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "TAjCC",
      "text": "\n$9.58$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "lSIhg",
      "text": "\n$4.79$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "VGCFP",
      "text": "\n$7.01$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "83EV4",
      "text": "\n$9.22$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "It is a salt of weak acid and weak base\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n& {\\left[\\mathrm{H}^{+}\\right]=\\sqrt{\\frac{\\mathrm{K}_{\\mathrm{w}} \\times \\mathrm{K}_{\\mathrm{a}}}{\\mathrm{K}_{\\mathrm{b}}}}} \\\\\n& \\mathrm{pH}=7.01\n\\end{aligned}\n$$",
    "image": null
  },
